/-!
# No rank analogue of the Shepherd-Leedham-Green-McKay theorem (Kourovka Notebook Problem 16.103)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.103 (E. I. Khukhro): suppose that `P` is a
`2`-generator finite `p`-group whose lower central quotients `γᵢ(P)/γᵢ₊₁(P)` are cyclic for all `i ≥
2`. Is it true that `P` contains a normal subgroup `N` of nilpotency class at most `2` such that the
rank of `P/N` is bounded in terms of `p` only?

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.103 (E. I.
Khukhro). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701294 (`KOU-16.103`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The rank of a finite group is the largest minimal number of generators of a subgroup; with the
minimal number of generators of `P/N` itself the question would be trivial, `P/N` being
`2`-generated. The source asks for a bound in terms of `p` only, i.e. a bound `r(p)` for each prime.
The target asks for one prime `p` with a bound `r` (the strongest true form, existential when
refuted, as in WantedExt/Sources/UnsolvedMath.md), so its refutation asserts that no prime has such
a bound: stronger than the source's negative answer, which needs one prime, and what Khukhro proves
(his Section 4 construction fixes an arbitrary prime `p` and, for every `r` and `l`, gives such a
group with no normal subgroup of derived length at most `l` and quotient of rank at most `r`; the
examples are unbounded for any fixed prime, Introduction). Class at most `2` is `γ₃(N) = 1`; `(⊤ :
Subgroup P).lowerCentralSeries j` is `γ_{j+1}(P)`.

The refutation constructs counterexamples at every prime using the positive Witt bracket.
A truncated Lie algebra admits a unipotent automorphism with one Jordan block. In a basis
adapted to this automorphism, scaling the bracket clears its denominators. Reduction modulo a
prime power and the class-three Baker–Campbell–Hausdorff formula give a finite group. The
semidirect product with the prime-power part of the automorphism has cyclic lower central
factors. Triple commutators force a large abelian section to survive in any quotient by a
class-two normal subgroup.
-/

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.RankAnalogueMaximalClassKourovka16Problem103Wanted

@[expose] public section

/-- **Minimal number of generators of a subgroup.** For a subgroup $H$ of a group $G$, the
minimal number of generators of $H$ is the least natural number $n$ such that $H$ is generated by
some finite set of $n$ elements of $G$; it is $0$ when $H$ is not finitely generated. -/
noncomputable def minGenerators {G : Type*} [Group G] (H : Subgroup G) : ℕ :=
  sInf {n | ∃ s : Finset G, s.card = n ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set G) = H}

/-- **Rank of a group.** The rank of a group $G$ is the supremum, in the natural numbers, of the
minimal numbers of generators of the subgroups of $G$, where an unbounded set of natural numbers
has supremum $0$. For a finite group $G$ it is the largest minimal number of generators of a
subgroup of $G$. -/
noncomputable def groupRank (G : Type*) [Group G] : ℕ :=
  sSup (Set.range (minGenerators (G := G)))

/-- **Cyclic lower central factors from the second on.** Let $\gamma_1(P) = P$ and
$\gamma_{i+1}(P) = [\gamma_i(P), P]$ be the lower central series of a group $P$. The group $P$
has cyclic lower central factors from the second on if for every $i \ge 2$ there is an element
$g \in \gamma_i(P)$ such that every $x \in \gamma_i(P)$ satisfies $x g^{-k} \in \gamma_{i+1}(P)$
for some integer $k$, that is, the factor $\gamma_i(P)/\gamma_{i+1}(P)$ is cyclic. -/
def HasCyclicLowerCentralFactorsFromSecond (P : Type*) [Group P] : Prop :=
  ∀ j : ℕ, 1 ≤ j → ∃ g ∈ (⊤ : Subgroup P).lowerCentralSeries j,
    ∀ x ∈ (⊤ : Subgroup P).lowerCentralSeries j,
      ∃ k : ℤ, x * (g ^ k)⁻¹ ∈ (⊤ : Subgroup P).lowerCentralSeries (j + 1)

/-- **Rank analogue of the Shepherd-Leedham-Green-McKay theorem (Kourovka 16.103).** The
statement that for some prime $p$ there is a natural number $r$ such that every finite $p$-group
$P$ generated by two elements whose lower central factors $\gamma_i(P)/\gamma_{i+1}(P)$ are
cyclic for all $i \ge 2$ has a normal subgroup $N$ of nilpotency class at most $2$ with $P/N$ of
rank at most $r$. Here $\gamma_1(P) = P$ and $\gamma_{i+1}(P) = [\gamma_i(P), P]$, and the rank
of a finite group is the largest minimal number of generators of its subgroups.

Kourovka 16.103 (E. I. Khukhro) asks for a bound $r(p)$ for each prime $p$; this form asks for
one prime, so its negation says that no prime has such a bound. -/
def rankAnalogueMaximalClass : Prop :=
  ∃ p : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ ∃ r : ℕ, ∀ (P : Type) [Group P] [Finite P], IsPGroup p P →
    (∃ x y : P, Subgroup.closure ({x, y} : Set P) = ⊤) → HasCyclicLowerCentralFactorsFromSecond P →
      ∃ N : Subgroup P, ∃ _ : N.Normal, N.lowerCentralSeries 2 = ⊥ ∧ groupRank (P ⧸ N) ≤ r

end

noncomputable section

/-! ## The truncated Witt Lie algebra -/

private abbrev Coordinates (R : Type*) (d : ℕ) := Fin (3 * d) → R

private def axis (R : Type*) [Zero R] [One R] (d i : ℕ) : Coordinates R d :=
  fun k ↦ if k.val = i then 1 else 0

private theorem axis_val {R : Type*} [Semiring R] {d i : ℕ} (hi : i < 3 * d) :
    axis R d i = Pi.basisFun R (Fin (3 * d)) ⟨i, hi⟩ := by
  ext k
  simp [axis, Pi.basisFun_apply, Pi.single_apply, Fin.ext_iff]

private theorem axis_eq_zero {R : Type*} [Semiring R] {d i : ℕ} (hi : 3 * d ≤ i) :
    axis R d i = 0 := by
  ext k
  simp [axis, (k.isLt.trans_le hi).ne]

private def bracket (d : ℕ) : Coordinates ℚ d →ₗ[ℚ] Coordinates ℚ d →ₗ[ℚ]
    Coordinates ℚ d :=
  (Pi.basisFun ℚ (Fin (3 * d))).constr ℚ fun i ↦
    (Pi.basisFun ℚ (Fin (3 * d))).constr ℚ fun j ↦
      ((j.val : ℚ) - i.val) • axis ℚ d (d + i.val + j.val)

private theorem bracket_axis (d i j : ℕ) : bracket d (axis ℚ d i) (axis ℚ d j) =
    ((j : ℚ) - i) • axis ℚ d (d + i + j) := by
  by_cases hi : i < 3 * d <;> by_cases hj : j < 3 * d
  · rw [axis_val hi, axis_val hj]
    simp [bracket]
  all_goals
    first | rw [axis_eq_zero (by omega : 3 * d ≤ i)] |
      rw [axis_eq_zero (by omega : 3 * d ≤ j)]
    rw [axis_eq_zero (by omega : 3 * d ≤ d + i + j)]
    simp

private theorem axis_induction {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {d : ℕ}
    (P : Coordinates R d → Prop) (x : Coordinates R d) (h₀ : P 0)
    (hadd : ∀ x y, P x → P y → P (x + y))
    (hsmul : ∀ (a : R) x, P x → P (a • x))
    (haxis : ∀ i : Fin (3 * d), P (axis R d i.val)) : P x := by
  let b := Pi.basisFun R (Fin (3 * d))
  have hmem : x ∈ Submodule.span R (Set.range b) := by rw [b.span_eq]; trivial
  induction hmem using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem z hz =>
    obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hz
    rw [← axis_val (R := R) i.isLt]
    exact haxis i
  | zero => exact h₀
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => exact hadd x y hx hy
  | smul a x _ hx => exact hsmul a x hx

private theorem bracket_skew (d : ℕ) (x y : Coordinates ℚ d) :
    bracket d x y = - bracket d y x := by
  have h : bracket d = -(bracket d).flip := by
    apply LinearMap.ext_basis (Pi.basisFun ℚ (Fin (3 * d))) (Pi.basisFun ℚ (Fin (3 * d)))
    intro i j
    rw [← axis_val i.isLt, ← axis_val j.isLt]
    simp only [LinearMap.neg_apply, LinearMap.flip_apply, bracket_axis, ← neg_smul]
    rw [show d + j.val + i.val = d + i.val + j.val by omega]
    congr 1
    ring
  change bracket d x y = (-(bracket d).flip) x y
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun (DFunLike.congr_fun h x) y

private theorem bracket_self (d : ℕ) (x : Coordinates ℚ d) : bracket d x x = 0 := by
  ext i
  have h := congr_fun (bracket_skew d x x) i
  change bracket d x x i = - bracket d x x i at h
  change bracket d x x i = 0
  linarith

private theorem bracket_jacobi (d : ℕ) (x y z : Coordinates ℚ d) :
    bracket d x (bracket d y z) =
      bracket d (bracket d x y) z + bracket d y (bracket d x z) := by
  induction x using axis_induction with
  | h₀ => simp
  | hadd x₁ x₂ h₁ h₂ => simp [h₁, h₂]; abel
  | hsmul a x hx => simp [hx, smul_add]
  | haxis i =>
    induction y using axis_induction with
    | h₀ => simp
    | hadd y₁ y₂ h₁ h₂ => simp [h₁, h₂]; abel
    | hsmul a y hy => simp [hy, smul_add]
    | haxis j =>
      induction z using axis_induction with
      | h₀ => simp
      | hadd z₁ z₂ h₁ h₂ => simp [h₁, h₂]; abel
      | hsmul a z hz => simp [hz, smul_add]
      | haxis k =>
        simp only [LinearMap.map_smul, LinearMap.smul_apply, bracket_axis, smul_smul]
        have h₁ : d + i.val + (d + j.val + k.val) = d + (d + i.val + j.val) + k.val := by omega
        have h₂ : d + j.val + (d + i.val + k.val) = d + (d + i.val + j.val) + k.val := by omega
        rw [h₁, h₂, ← add_smul]
        congr 1
        push_cast
        ring

private local instance instRationalLieRing (d : ℕ) : LieRing (Coordinates ℚ d) where
  bracket x y := bracket d x y
  add_lie x y z := by change bracket d (x + y) z = _; simp
  lie_add x y z := (bracket d x).map_add y z
  lie_self := bracket_self d
  leibniz_lie := bracket_jacobi d

private local instance instRationalLieAlgebra (d : ℕ) : LieAlgebra ℚ (Coordinates ℚ d) where
  lie_smul a x y := (bracket d x).map_smul a y

private def shiftFun (d : ℕ) (x : Coordinates ℚ d) (k : Fin (3 * d)) : ℚ :=
  if h : k.val = 0 then 0 else
    ((d : ℚ) + ((k.val - 1 : ℕ) : ℚ) - 1) * x ⟨k.val - 1, by omega⟩

private def shift (d : ℕ) : Coordinates ℚ d →ₗ[ℚ] Coordinates ℚ d where
  toFun x := shiftFun d x
  map_add' x y := by ext k; by_cases h : k.val = 0 <;> simp [shiftFun, h, mul_add]
  map_smul' a x := by
    ext k
    by_cases hk : k.val = 0 <;> simp [shiftFun, hk, mul_left_comm]

private theorem shift_axis (d i : ℕ) :
    shift d (axis ℚ d i) = ((d : ℚ) + i - 1) • axis ℚ d (i + 1) := by
  ext k
  change shiftFun d (axis ℚ d i) k = _
  by_cases h : k.val = 0
  · simp [shiftFun, axis, h]
  · by_cases h' : k.val = i + 1
    · simp [shiftFun, axis, h']
    · have h'' : k.val - 1 ≠ i := by omega
      simp [shiftFun, axis, h, h', h'']

private theorem shift_leibniz (d : ℕ) (x y : Coordinates ℚ d) :
    shift d (bracket d x y) = bracket d (shift d x) y + bracket d x (shift d y) := by
  induction x using axis_induction with
  | h₀ => simp
  | hadd x₁ x₂ h₁ h₂ => simp [h₁, h₂]; abel
  | hsmul a x hx => simp [hx, smul_add]
  | haxis i =>
    induction y using axis_induction with
    | h₀ => simp
    | hadd y₁ y₂ h₁ h₂ => simp [h₁, h₂]; abel
    | hsmul a y hy => simp [hy, smul_add]
    | haxis j =>
      simp only [LinearMap.map_smul, LinearMap.smul_apply, bracket_axis, shift_axis, smul_smul]
      rw [show d + (i.val + 1) + j.val = d + i.val + j.val + 1 by omega,
        show d + i.val + (j.val + 1) = d + i.val + j.val + 1 by omega, ← add_smul]
      congr 1
      push_cast
      ring

private def derivation (d : ℕ) : LieDerivation ℚ (Coordinates ℚ d) (Coordinates ℚ d) where
  toLinearMap := shift d
  leibniz' x y := by
    change shift d (bracket d x y) = bracket d x (shift d y) - bracket d y (shift d x)
    rw [shift_leibniz, bracket_skew d y (shift d x), sub_neg_eq_add, add_comm]

/-! ## A basis adapted to the unipotent shift -/

private def Tail {R : Type*} [Zero R] {d : ℕ} (n : ℕ) (x : Coordinates R d) : Prop :=
  ∀ k : Fin (3 * d), k.val < n → x k = 0

private theorem tail_of_le {R : Type*} [Zero R] {d m n : ℕ} {x : Coordinates R d}
    (hmn : m ≤ n) (hx : Tail n x) : Tail m x := fun k hk ↦ hx k (hk.trans_le hmn)

private theorem tail_shift {d m : ℕ} {x : Coordinates ℚ d} (hx : Tail m x) :
    Tail (m + 1) (shift d x) := by
  intro k hk
  change shiftFun d x k = 0
  by_cases h : k.val = 0
  · simp [shiftFun, h]
  · have hk' : k.val - 1 < m := by omega
    rw [shiftFun, dite_eq_right h, hx ⟨k.val - 1, by omega⟩ hk', mul_zero]

private theorem shift_leading {d i : ℕ} (hi : i + 1 < 3 * d) (x : Coordinates ℚ d) :
    shift d x ⟨i + 1, hi⟩ = ((d : ℚ) + i - 1) * x ⟨i, by omega⟩ := by
  simp [shift, shiftFun]

private theorem tail_shift_pow {d m : ℕ} {x : Coordinates ℚ d} (hx : Tail m x) (a : ℕ) :
    Tail (m + a) ((shift d ^ a) x) := by
  induction a with
  | zero => simpa using hx
  | succ a ih =>
    rw [pow_succ', mul_apply_eq_comp]
    exact tail_shift ih

private theorem shift_nilpotent (d : ℕ) : shift d ^ (3 * d) = 0 := by
  ext x k
  exact tail_shift_pow (m := 0) (fun _ h ↦ (Nat.not_lt_zero _ h).elim) (3 * d) k
    (by simp)

private def raise (d : ℕ) : Module.End ℚ (Coordinates ℚ d) :=
  IsNilpotent.exp (shift d) - 1

private theorem exp_remainder {d m : ℕ} {x : Coordinates ℚ d} (hx : Tail m x) :
    Tail (m + 2) (raise d x - shift d x) := by
  have hn : shift d ^ (3 * d + 2) = 0 := pow_eq_zero_of_le (by omega) (shift_nilpotent d)
  rw [raise, IsNilpotent.exp_eq_sum hn, ← Finset.sum_range_add_sum_Ico _ (by omega : 2 ≤ 3 * d + 2)]
  simp only [Finset.sum_range_succ, Finset.sum_range_zero, zero_add, LinearMap.sub_apply,
    LinearMap.add_apply, LinearMap.sum_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, one_apply_eq_self,
    pow_zero, pow_one, Nat.factorial_zero, Nat.factorial_one, Nat.cast_one, inv_one, one_smul]
  intro k hk
  simp only [Pi.sub_apply, Pi.add_apply, Finset.sum_apply]
  rw [Finset.sum_eq_zero (fun a ha ↦ ?_)]
  · abel
  simp only [Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
  have ha' := (Finset.mem_Ico.mp ha).1
  rw [tail_shift_pow hx a k (by omega), mul_zero]

private theorem tail_raise {d m : ℕ} {x : Coordinates ℚ d} (hx : Tail m x) :
    Tail (m + 1) (raise d x) := by
  intro k hk
  have h₁ := exp_remainder hx k (by omega)
  have h₂ := tail_shift hx k hk
  change raise d x k - shift d x k = 0 at h₁
  linarith

private theorem raise_leading {d i : ℕ} (hi : i + 1 < 3 * d) {x : Coordinates ℚ d}
    (hx : Tail i x) :
    raise d x ⟨i + 1, hi⟩ = ((d : ℚ) + i - 1) * x ⟨i, by omega⟩ := by
  have h₁ := exp_remainder hx ⟨i + 1, hi⟩ (by simp)
  change raise d x ⟨i + 1, hi⟩ - shift d x ⟨i + 1, hi⟩ = 0 at h₁
  rw [shift_leading] at h₁
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp h₁

private def raisedAxis (d i : ℕ) : Coordinates ℚ d :=
  (raise d ^ i) (axis ℚ d 0)

private theorem raisedAxis_succ (d i : ℕ) : raisedAxis d (i + 1) = raise d (raisedAxis d i) := by
  rw [raisedAxis, pow_succ', mul_apply_eq_comp, raisedAxis]

private theorem tail_raisedAxis (d i : ℕ) : Tail i (raisedAxis d i) := by
  induction i with
  | zero => intro k hk; omega
  | succ i ih => rw [raisedAxis_succ]; exact tail_raise ih

private theorem raisedAxis_pos {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (i : ℕ) (hi : i < 3 * d) :
    0 < raisedAxis d i ⟨i, hi⟩ := by
  induction i with
  | zero => simp [raisedAxis, axis]
  | succ i ih =>
    rw [raisedAxis_succ, raise_leading hi (tail_raisedAxis d i)]
    apply mul_pos _ (ih (by omega))
    have hd' : (2 : ℚ) ≤ d := by exact_mod_cast hd
    have hi' : (0 : ℚ) ≤ i := by positivity
    linarith

private theorem triangular_sum {d : ℕ} (f : Fin (3 * d) → ℚ) (i : Fin (3 * d))
    (hf : ∀ j : Fin (3 * d), j.val < i.val → f j = 0) :
    (∑ j : Fin (3 * d), f j • raisedAxis d j.val) i = f i * raisedAxis d i.val i := by
  rw [Finset.sum_apply, Finset.sum_eq_single i]
  · rfl
  · intro j _ hji
    rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne (fun h ↦ hji (Fin.ext h)) with h | h
    · simp [hf j h]
    · simp [tail_raisedAxis d j.val i h]
  · simp

private theorem raisedAxis_independent {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) :
    LinearIndependent ℚ (fun i : Fin (3 * d) ↦ raisedAxis d i.val) := by
  rw [Fintype.linearIndependent_iffₛ]
  intro f g h i
  have hh : ∑ j : Fin (3 * d), (f j - g j) • raisedAxis d j.val = 0 := by
    simp_rw [sub_smul, Finset.sum_sub_distrib, h, sub_self]
  suffices ∀ k : ℕ, ∀ hk : k < 3 * d, f ⟨k, hk⟩ - g ⟨k, hk⟩ = 0 by
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp (this i.val i.isLt)
  intro k
  induction k using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | ind k ih =>
    intro hk
    have hcoord := congr_fun hh ⟨k, hk⟩
    change (∑ j : Fin (3 * d), (f - g) j • raisedAxis d j.val) ⟨k, hk⟩ = 0 at hcoord
    rw [triangular_sum (f - g) ⟨k, hk⟩ (fun j hj ↦ ih j.val hj j.isLt)] at hcoord
    exact (mul_eq_zero.mp hcoord).resolve_right (raisedAxis_pos hd k hk).ne'

private def shiftedBasis {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) :
    Module.Basis (Fin (3 * d)) ℚ (Coordinates ℚ d) :=
  basisOfLinearIndependentOfCardEqFinrank' _ (raisedAxis_independent hd)
    (Module.finrank_fintype_fun_eq_card ℚ).symm

private theorem shiftedBasis_apply {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (i : Fin (3 * d)) :
    shiftedBasis hd i = raisedAxis d i.val := by simp [shiftedBasis]

private theorem bracket_coords {d : ℕ} (x y : Coordinates ℚ d) (k : Fin (3 * d)) :
    bracket d x y k =
      ∑ i : Fin (3 * d), ∑ j : Fin (3 * d),
        if d + i.val + j.val = k.val then x i * y j * ((j.val : ℚ) - i.val) else 0 := by
  classical
  simp only [bracket, Module.Basis.constr_apply_fintype,
    LinearMap.sum_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, Finset.sum_apply, Pi.smul_apply,
    smul_eq_mul, Finset.mul_sum, axis]
  apply Finset.sum_congr rfl
  intro i _
  apply Finset.sum_congr rfl
  intro j _
  by_cases h : d + i.val + j.val = k.val
  · simp [h, mul_assoc]
  · simp [h, Ne.symm h]

private theorem bracket_tail {d m n : ℕ} {x y : Coordinates ℚ d}
    (hx : Tail m x) (hy : Tail n y) : Tail (d + m + n) (bracket d x y) := by
  intro k hk
  rw [bracket_coords]
  apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
  intro i _
  apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
  intro j _
  by_cases h : d + i.val + j.val = k.val
  · by_cases hi : i.val < m
    · simp [hx i hi]
    · have hj : j.val < n := by omega
      simp [hy j hj]
  · simp [h]

private theorem bracket_leading {d : ℕ} {i j k : Fin (3 * d)} {x y : Coordinates ℚ d}
    (hx : Tail i.val x) (hy : Tail j.val y) (hk : d + i.val + j.val = k.val) :
    bracket d x y k = x i * y j * ((j.val : ℚ) - i.val) := by
  classical
  rw [bracket_coords, Finset.sum_eq_single i, Finset.sum_eq_single j, ite_eq_left hk]
  · intro l _ hlj
    by_cases h : l.val < j.val
    · simp [hy l h]
    · rw [ite_eq_right]
      have hne : l.val ≠ j.val := fun hh ↦ hlj (Fin.ext hh)
      omega
  · simp
  · intro l _ hli
    apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
    intro q _
    by_cases hl : l.val < i.val
    · simp [hx l hl]
    by_cases hq : q.val < j.val
    · simp [hy q hq]
    · rw [ite_eq_right]
      have hne : l.val ≠ i.val := fun hh ↦ hli (Fin.ext hh)
      omega
  · simp

private theorem repr_tail {d n : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) {x : Coordinates ℚ d} (hx : Tail n x) :
    Tail n (fun i ↦ (shiftedBasis hd).repr x i) := by
  have h := (shiftedBasis hd).sum_repr x
  simp_rw [shiftedBasis_apply] at h
  suffices ∀ k : ℕ, ∀ hk : k < 3 * d, k < n → (shiftedBasis hd).repr x ⟨k, hk⟩ = 0 by
    exact fun k hk ↦ this k.val k.isLt hk
  intro k
  induction k using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | ind k ih =>
    intro hk hkn
    have hc := congr_fun h ⟨k, hk⟩
    rw [triangular_sum _ _ (fun j hj ↦ ih j.val hj j.isLt (hj.trans hkn)), hx _ hkn] at hc
    exact (mul_eq_zero.mp hc).resolve_right (raisedAxis_pos hd k hk).ne'

private theorem repr_leading {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) {k : Fin (3 * d)}
    {x : Coordinates ℚ d} (hx : Tail k.val x) :
    (shiftedBasis hd).repr x k * raisedAxis d k.val k = x k := by
  have h := (shiftedBasis hd).sum_repr x
  simp_rw [shiftedBasis_apply] at h
  have hc := congr_fun h k
  rw [triangular_sum _ _ (repr_tail hd hx)] at hc
  exact hc

private def coeffs {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (i j k : Fin (3 * d)) : ℚ :=
  (shiftedBasis hd).repr (bracket d (raisedAxis d i.val) (raisedAxis d j.val)) k

private theorem coeffs_zero {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (i j k : Fin (3 * d))
    (hk : k.val < d + i.val + j.val) : coeffs hd i j k = 0 :=
  repr_tail hd (bracket_tail (tail_raisedAxis d i.val) (tail_raisedAxis d j.val)) k hk

private theorem coeffs_lead_nonzero {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) {i j k : Fin (3 * d)}
    (hk : k.val = d + i.val + j.val) (hij : i ≠ j) : coeffs hd i j k ≠ 0 := by
  have h := repr_leading hd
    (tail_of_le hk.le (bracket_tail (tail_raisedAxis d i.val) (tail_raisedAxis d j.val)))
  change coeffs hd i j k * raisedAxis d k.val k = _ at h
  rw [bracket_leading (tail_raisedAxis d i.val) (tail_raisedAxis d j.val) hk.symm] at h
  have hn : ((j.val : ℚ) - i.val) ≠ 0 := by
    apply sub_ne_zero.mpr
    exact_mod_cast (show j.val ≠ i.val from fun he ↦ hij (Fin.ext he.symm))
  intro hc
  rw [hc, zero_mul] at h
  have hprod := mul_ne_zero (raisedAxis_pos hd _ i.isLt).ne' (raisedAxis_pos hd _ j.isLt).ne'
  exact (mul_ne_zero hprod hn) h.symm

/-! ## Integral structure constants and reduction -/

private abbrev Tensor (R : Type*) (d : ℕ) := Fin (3 * d) → Fin (3 * d) → Coordinates R d

private def tensorLin {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {d : ℕ} (C : Tensor R d) :
    Coordinates R d →ₗ[R] Coordinates R d →ₗ[R] Coordinates R d :=
  (Pi.basisFun R (Fin (3 * d))).constr R fun i ↦ (Pi.basisFun R (Fin (3 * d))).constr R (C i)

private theorem tensorLin_apply {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {d : ℕ}
    (C : Tensor R d) (x y : Coordinates R d) (k : Fin (3 * d)) :
    tensorLin C x y k = ∑ i, ∑ j, x i * y j * C i j k := by
  simp [tensorLin, Module.Basis.constr_apply_fintype, Finset.mul_sum, mul_assoc]

private def step {R : Type*} [Zero R] {d : ℕ} (x : Coordinates R d) (k : Fin (3 * d)) : R :=
  if k.val = 0 then 0 else x ⟨k.val - 1, by omega⟩

private def stepLin {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (d : ℕ) : Module.End R (Coordinates R d) where
  toFun := step
  map_add' x y := by ext k; by_cases h : k.val = 0 <;> simp [step, h]
  map_smul' r x := by ext k; by_cases h : k.val = 0 <;> simp [step, h]

private theorem step_axis {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {d i : ℕ} :
    step (axis R d i) = axis R d (i + 1) := by
  ext k
  by_cases h : k.val = 0
  · simp [step, axis, h]
  have h₁ : k.val - 1 = i ↔ k.val = i + 1 := by omega
  simp [step, axis, h, h₁]

private theorem iso_axis {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (i : ℕ) :
    (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm (axis ℚ d i) = raisedAxis d i := by
  by_cases hi : i < 3 * d
  · let i' : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨i, hi⟩
    change (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm (axis ℚ d i) = raisedAxis d i'.val
    rw [← shiftedBasis_apply hd i']
    apply (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.injective
    rw [LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    ext k
    simp [axis, Fin.ext_iff, i', eq_comm]
  · have hz : raisedAxis d i = 0 := by
      ext k
      exact tail_raisedAxis d i k (by omega)
    rw [axis_eq_zero (by omega : 3 * d ≤ i), map_zero, hz]

private def raiseAut (d : ℕ) : Coordinates ℚ d ≃ₗ⁅ℚ⁆ Coordinates ℚ d :=
  (derivation d).exp ⟨3 * d, by change shift d ^ (3 * d) = 0; exact shift_nilpotent d⟩

private theorem raiseAut_apply (d : ℕ) (x : Coordinates ℚ d) :
    raiseAut d x = IsNilpotent.exp (shift d) x := by
  exact LieDerivation.exp_map_apply (derivation d) _ x

private theorem iso_T {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (x : Coordinates ℚ d) :
    (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm (x + step x) =
      (raiseAut d)
        ((shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm x) := by
  induction x using axis_induction with
  | h₀ =>
    have : step (0 : Coordinates ℚ d) = 0 := (stepLin (R := ℚ) d).map_zero
    rw [this, add_zero, map_zero, map_zero]
  | hadd x y hx hy =>
    have : step (x + y) = step x + step y := (stepLin (R := ℚ) d).map_add x y
    rw [this, show x + y + (step x + step y) = x + step x + (y + step y) by abel,
      map_add, hx, hy, map_add, map_add]
  | hsmul a x hx =>
    have : step (a • x) = a • step x := (stepLin (R := ℚ) d).map_smul a x
    rw [this, ← smul_add, map_smul, hx, map_smul, map_smul]
  | haxis i =>
    rw [step_axis, map_add, iso_axis, iso_axis, raisedAxis_succ, raiseAut_apply]
    simp [raise]

private theorem iso_bracket {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (x y : Coordinates ℚ d) :
    (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm (tensorLin (coeffs hd) x y) =
      bracket d ((shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm x) ((shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm y) := by
  let E := (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm
  change E (tensorLin (coeffs hd) x y) = bracket d (E x) (E y)
  have h : (tensorLin (coeffs hd)).compr₂ E.toLinearMap =
      ((bracket d).compl₁₂ E.toLinearMap E.toLinearMap) := by
    apply LinearMap.ext_basis (Pi.basisFun ℚ (Fin (3 * d))) (Pi.basisFun ℚ (Fin (3 * d)))
    intro i j
    rw [← axis_val i.isLt, ← axis_val j.isLt]
    change E (tensorLin (coeffs hd) (axis ℚ d i.val) (axis ℚ d j.val)) =
      bracket d (E (axis ℚ d i.val)) (E (axis ℚ d j.val))
    rw [iso_axis hd, iso_axis hd, axis_val i.isLt, axis_val j.isLt]
    simp only [tensorLin, Module.Basis.constr_basis]
    exact (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm_apply_apply _
  simpa only [LinearMap.compr₂_apply, LinearMap.compl₁₂_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe] using
    DFunLike.congr_fun (DFunLike.congr_fun h x) y

private theorem clear_denominators {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (v : ι → ℚ) :
    ∃ a : ℕ, a ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ C : ι → ℤ, ∀ i, (C i : ℚ) = (a : ℚ) * v i := by
  classical
  let := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  let a : ℕ := ∏ i, (v i).den
  have ha : a ≠ 0 := Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.mpr fun i _ ↦ (v i).den_ne_zero
  have hdvd (i : ι) : (v i).den ∣ a :=
    Finset.dvd_prod_of_mem (fun j ↦ (v j).den) (Finset.mem_univ i)
  let w (i : ι) : ℕ := (hdvd i).choose
  have hw (i : ι) : a = (v i).den * w i := (hdvd i).choose_spec
  refine ⟨a, ha, fun i ↦ (w i : ℤ) * (v i).num, ?_⟩
  intro i
  have hden : ((v i).den : ℚ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr (v i).den_ne_zero
  have hc : v i * (v i).den = (v i).num := (eq_div_iff hden).mp (Rat.num_div_den (v i)).symm
  have ha' := congrArg (fun n : ℕ ↦ (n : ℚ)) (hw i)
  change (a : ℚ) = (((v i).den * w i : ℕ) : ℚ) at ha'
  rw [Nat.cast_mul] at ha'
  rw [Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_natCast, ha', ← hc]
  ring

private theorem exists_integer_tensor {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) :
    ∃ a : ℚ, a ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ C : Tensor ℤ d,
      ∀ i j k, (C i j k : ℚ) = a * coeffs hd i j k := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, C, hC⟩ := clear_denominators
    (fun x : Fin (3 * d) × Fin (3 * d) × Fin (3 * d) ↦ coeffs hd x.1 x.2.1 x.2.2)
  exact ⟨(a : ℚ), Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr ha, fun i j k ↦ C (i, j, k), fun i j k ↦ hC (i, j, k)⟩

private def tensorMap {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] {d : ℕ}
    (f : R →+* S) (C : Tensor R d) : Tensor S d := fun i j k ↦ f (C i j k)

private def coordsMap {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] {d : ℕ}
    (f : R →+* S) (x : Coordinates R d) : Coordinates S d := fun i ↦ f (x i)

private theorem coordsMap_bracket {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] {d : ℕ}
    (f : R →+* S) (C : Tensor R d) (x y : Coordinates R d) :
    coordsMap f (tensorLin C x y) = tensorLin (tensorMap f C) (coordsMap f x) (coordsMap f y) := by
  ext k
  simp [coordsMap, tensorLin_apply, tensorMap, map_mul]

private theorem coordsMap_step {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] {d : ℕ}
    (f : R →+* S) (x : Coordinates R d) :
    coordsMap f (step x) = step (coordsMap f x) := by
  ext k
  by_cases h : k.val = 0 <;> simp [coordsMap, step, h]

private theorem coordsMap_add {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] {d : ℕ}
    (f : R →+* S) (x y : Coordinates R d) :
    coordsMap f (x + y) = coordsMap f x + coordsMap f y := by ext; simp [coordsMap]

private structure IntegralTable (d : ℕ) where
  entries : Tensor ℤ d
  supported : ∀ i j k, k.val < d + i.val + j.val → entries i j k = 0
  leading : 2 ≤ d → ∀ i j k, k.val = d + i.val + j.val → i ≠ j → entries i j k ≠ 0
  alternating : ∀ x, tensorLin entries x x = 0
  jacobi : ∀ x y z, tensorLin entries x (tensorLin entries y z) =
    tensorLin entries (tensorLin entries x y) z + tensorLin entries y (tensorLin entries x z)
  shift_bracket : ∀ x y, tensorLin entries x y + step (tensorLin entries x y) =
    tensorLin entries (x + step x) (y + step y)

private theorem exists_integralTable {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) : Nonempty (IntegralTable d) := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, C, hC⟩ := exists_integer_tensor hd
  let E := (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm
  let Q : ℤ →+* ℚ := Int.castRingHom ℚ
  have hQ : Function.Injective (coordsMap (d := d) Q) := fun x y h ↦
    funext fun k ↦ Int.cast_injective (congr_fun h k)
  have hE (x y : Coordinates ℚ d) :
      E (tensorLin (tensorMap Q C) x y) = a • bracket d (E x) (E y) := by
    have h : tensorLin (tensorMap Q C) x y = a • tensorLin (coeffs hd) x y := by
      ext k
      simp only [tensorLin_apply, tensorMap, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ ↦ by
        change x i * y j * (C i j k : ℚ) = _
        rw [hC]
        ring
    rw [h, map_smul, iso_bracket hd]
  refine ⟨⟨C, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · intro i j k h
    apply Int.cast_injective (α := ℚ)
    rw [hC, coeffs_zero hd _ _ _ h, mul_zero, Int.cast_zero]
  · intro _ i j k h hij hz
    have hc := hC i j k
    rw [hz, Int.cast_zero] at hc
    exact (mul_ne_zero ha (coeffs_lead_nonzero hd h hij)) hc.symm
  · intro x
    apply hQ
    apply E.injective
    rw [coordsMap_bracket, hE, bracket_self, smul_zero]
    exact (map_zero E).symm.trans (congrArg E (by ext k; simp [coordsMap]))
  · intro x y z
    apply hQ
    apply E.injective
    simp only [coordsMap_bracket, coordsMap_add, map_add, hE,
      LinearMap.map_smul, LinearMap.smul_apply, smul_smul]
    rw [bracket_jacobi, smul_add]
  · intro x y
    apply hQ
    apply E.injective
    simp only [coordsMap_add, coordsMap_step, coordsMap_bracket]
    change (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm (_ + step _) =
      E (tensorLin (tensorMap Q C) _ _)
    rw [iso_T hd, hE, hE]
    change (raiseAut d) (a • ⁅E (coordsMap Q x), E (coordsMap Q y)⁆) =
      a • ⁅(shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm (_ + step _),
        (shiftedBasis hd).equivFun.symm (_ + step _)⁆
    rw [map_smul, LieEquiv.map_lie, iso_T hd, iso_T hd]

private def integralTable (d : ℕ) : IntegralTable d :=
  if h : 2 ≤ d then Classical.choice (exists_integralTable h) else
    ⟨0, fun _ _ _ _ ↦ rfl, fun hd ↦ (h hd).elim,
      fun _ ↦ by ext k; simp [tensorLin_apply],
      fun _ _ _ ↦ by ext k; simp [tensorLin_apply],
      fun _ _ ↦ by ext k; simp [tensorLin_apply, step]⟩

private theorem coordsMap_surjective {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] {d : ℕ}
    (f : R →+* S) (hf : Function.Surjective f) : Function.Surjective (coordsMap (d := d) f) := by
  intro x
  choose y hy using fun k ↦ hf (x k)
  exact ⟨y, funext hy⟩

private def finiteBracket (d q : ℕ) : Coordinates (ZMod q) d →ₗ[ZMod q]
    Coordinates (ZMod q) d →ₗ[ZMod q] Coordinates (ZMod q) d :=
  tensorLin (tensorMap (Int.castRingHom (ZMod q)) (integralTable d).entries)

private theorem cast_finiteBracket {d q : ℕ} (x y : Coordinates ℤ d) :
    coordsMap (Int.castRingHom (ZMod q)) (tensorLin (integralTable d).entries x y) =
      finiteBracket d q (coordsMap (Int.castRingHom (ZMod q)) x)
        (coordsMap (Int.castRingHom (ZMod q)) y) :=
  coordsMap_bracket _ _ _ _

private theorem zmod_coords_surjective (d q : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (coordsMap (d := d) (Int.castRingHom (ZMod q))) :=
  coordsMap_surjective _ (ZMod.intCast_surjective (n := q))

private theorem finiteBracket_self {d q : ℕ} (x : Coordinates (ZMod q) d) :
    finiteBracket d q x x = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := zmod_coords_surjective d q x
  rw [← cast_finiteBracket, (integralTable d).alternating]
  ext k
  simp [coordsMap]

private theorem finiteBracket_jacobi {d q : ℕ} (x y z : Coordinates (ZMod q) d) :
    finiteBracket d q x (finiteBracket d q y z) =
      finiteBracket d q (finiteBracket d q x y) z +
        finiteBracket d q y (finiteBracket d q x z) := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := zmod_coords_surjective d q x
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := zmod_coords_surjective d q y
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := zmod_coords_surjective d q z
  simp only [← cast_finiteBracket, ← coordsMap_add]
  rw [(integralTable d).jacobi]

private theorem finiteBracket_shift {d q : ℕ} (x y : Coordinates (ZMod q) d) :
    finiteBracket d q x y + step (finiteBracket d q x y) =
      finiteBracket d q (x + step x) (y + step y) := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := zmod_coords_surjective d q x
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := zmod_coords_surjective d q y
  simpa only [coordsMap_add, coordsMap_step, cast_finiteBracket] using
    congrArg (coordsMap (Int.castRingHom (ZMod q))) ((integralTable d).shift_bracket x y)

private local instance instResidueLieRing (d q : ℕ) : LieRing (Coordinates (ZMod q) d) where
  bracket x y := finiteBracket d q x y
  add_lie x y z := by change finiteBracket d q (x + y) z = _; simp
  lie_add x y z := (finiteBracket d q x).map_add y z
  lie_self := finiteBracket_self
  leibniz_lie := finiteBracket_jacobi

private theorem tensor_supported {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {d m n : ℕ} {C : Tensor R d}
    (hC : ∀ i j k, k.val < d + i.val + j.val → C i j k = 0)
    {x y : Coordinates R d} (hx : Tail m x) (hy : Tail n y) :
    Tail (d + m + n) (tensorLin C x y) := by
  intro k hk
  rw [tensorLin_apply]
  apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
  intro i _
  apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
  intro j _
  by_cases hi : i.val < m
  · simp [hx i hi]
  by_cases hj : j.val < n
  · simp [hy j hj]
  simp [hC i j k (by omega)]

private theorem finiteBracket_tail {d q m n : ℕ} {x y : Coordinates (ZMod q) d}
    (hx : Tail m x) (hy : Tail n y) : Tail (d + m + n) ⁅x, y⁆ := by
  change Tail (d + m + n) (finiteBracket d q x y)
  exact tensor_supported (fun i j k hk ↦
    show ((integralTable d).entries i j k : ZMod q) = 0 by
      rw [(integralTable d).supported i j k hk, Int.cast_zero]) hx hy

private theorem finiteBracket_lead {d q : ℕ} {i j k : Fin (3 * d)}
    {x y : Coordinates (ZMod q) d} (hx : Tail i.val x) (hy : Tail j.val y)
    (hk : k.val = d + i.val + j.val) :
    ⁅x, y⁆ k = x i * y j * ((integralTable d).entries i j k : ZMod q) := by
  change tensorLin (tensorMap (Int.castRingHom (ZMod q)) (integralTable d).entries) x y k = _
  rw [tensorLin_apply, Finset.sum_eq_single i, Finset.sum_eq_single j]
  · rfl
  · intro l _ hlj
    by_cases hl : l.val < j.val
    · simp [hy l hl]
    have hne : l.val ≠ j.val := fun he ↦ hlj (Fin.ext he)
    simp [tensorMap, (integralTable d).supported i l k (by omega)]
  · simp
  · intro l _ hli
    apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
    intro t _
    by_cases hl : l.val < i.val
    · simp [hx l hl]
    by_cases ht : t.val < j.val
    · simp [hy t ht]
    have hne : l.val ≠ i.val := fun he ↦ hli (Fin.ext he)
    simp [tensorMap, (integralTable d).supported l t k (by omega)]
  · simp

/-! ## A group law in nilpotency class at most three -/

private def ClassThree (L : Type*) [LieRing L] : Prop :=
  ∀ x y z w : L, ⁅x, ⁅y, ⁅z, w⁆⁆⁆ = 0

variable {L : Type*} [LieRing L]

private theorem bracket_four_nested (h : ClassThree L) (x y z w : L) :
    ⁅x, ⁅y, ⁅z, w⁆⁆⁆ = 0 := h x y z w

private theorem bracket_four (h : ClassThree L) (x y z w : L) :
    ⁅⁅x, y⁆, ⁅z, w⁆⁆ = 0 := by
  rw [← sub_eq_of_eq_add (leibniz_lie x y ⁅z, w⁆), h, h, sub_zero]

private theorem bracket_four_middle (h : ClassThree L) (x y z w : L) :
    ⁅x, ⁅⁅y, z⁆, w⁆⁆ = 0 := by rw [← lie_skew ⁅y, z⁆ w, lie_neg, bracket_four_nested h, neg_zero]

private theorem bracket_four_left (h : ClassThree L) (x y z w : L) :
    ⁅⁅x, ⁅y, z⁆⁆, w⁆ = 0 := by rw [← lie_skew ⁅x, ⁅y, z⁆⁆ w, bracket_four_nested h, neg_zero]

private theorem bracket_four_left' (h : ClassThree L) (x y z w : L) :
    ⁅⁅⁅x, y⁆, z⁆, w⁆ = 0 := by rw [← lie_skew ⁅x, y⁆ z, neg_lie, bracket_four_left h, neg_zero]

private def bchMul (x y : L) : L :=
  x + y + 6 • ⁅x, y⁆ + 12 • ⁅x, ⁅x, y⁆⁆ + 12 • ⁅y, ⁅y, x⁆⁆

private theorem bch_assoc (h : ClassThree L) (x y z : L) :
    bchMul (bchMul x y) z = bchMul x (bchMul y z) := by
  simp only [bchMul, add_lie, lie_add, nsmul_lie, lie_nsmul, bracket_four_nested h,
    bracket_four h, bracket_four_left h, bracket_four_middle h, add_zero,
    nsmul_zero, smul_add, smul_smul]
  have hz : ⁅z, ⁅y, x⁆⁆ = ⁅⁅x, y⁆, z⁆ := by
    rw [← lie_skew y x, lie_neg, lie_skew]
  rw [hz, ← lie_skew z x, lie_neg, lie_neg, lie_lie]
  abel

private structure BCH (L : Type*) where
  val : L

private instance instBCHGroup [h : Fact (ClassThree L)] : Group (BCH L) where
  mul x y := ⟨bchMul x.val y.val⟩
  one := ⟨0⟩
  inv x := ⟨-x.val⟩
  mul_assoc x y z := congrArg BCH.mk (bch_assoc h.out x.val y.val z.val)
  one_mul x := by change BCH.mk (bchMul 0 x.val) = x; simp [bchMul]
  mul_one x := by change BCH.mk (bchMul x.val 0) = x; simp [bchMul]
  inv_mul_cancel x := by change BCH.mk (bchMul (-x.val) x.val) = BCH.mk 0; simp [bchMul]

open scoped commutatorElement

private theorem bch_commutator [h : Fact (ClassThree L)] (x y : BCH L) :
    (⁅x, y⁆ : BCH L).val = 12 • ⁅x.val, y.val⁆ + 72 • ⁅x.val + y.val, ⁅x.val, y.val⁆⁆ := by
  change bchMul (bchMul (bchMul x.val y.val) (-x.val)) (-y.val) = _
  simp only [bchMul, add_lie, lie_add, nsmul_lie, lie_nsmul, bracket_four_nested h.out,
    bracket_four h.out, bracket_four_left h.out, bracket_four_middle h.out,
    lie_self, neg_lie, lie_neg, add_zero, zero_add,
    nsmul_zero, smul_add, smul_smul, neg_zero, neg_add_rev, smul_neg]
  rw [← lie_skew y.val x.val]
  simp only [lie_neg, neg_lie, neg_neg, smul_neg, bracket_four_left' h.out]
  rw [← lie_skew ⁅x.val, y.val⁆ x.val, ← lie_skew ⁅x.val, y.val⁆ y.val]
  abel

/-! ## The finite group and its lower central series -/

private theorem tail_zero {R : Type*} [Zero R] {d n : ℕ} :
    Tail n (0 : Coordinates R d) := fun _ _ ↦ rfl

private theorem tail_trivial {R : Type*} [Zero R] {d : ℕ} (x : Coordinates R d) :
    Tail 0 x := fun _ h ↦ (Nat.not_lt_zero _ h).elim

private theorem tail_add {R : Type*} [AddZeroClass R] {d n : ℕ} {x y : Coordinates R d}
    (hx : Tail n x) (hy : Tail n y) : Tail n (x + y) := by
  intro i hi
  simp [hx i hi, hy i hi]

private theorem tail_neg {R : Type*} [AddGroup R] {d n : ℕ} {x : Coordinates R d}
    (hx : Tail n x) : Tail n (-x) := by
  intro i hi
  simp [hx i hi]

private theorem tail_nsmul {R : Type*} [AddMonoid R] {d n : ℕ} {x : Coordinates R d}
    (hx : Tail n x) (c : ℕ) : Tail n (c • x) := by
  intro i hi
  simp [hx i hi]

private theorem finiteClassThree (d q : ℕ) : ClassThree (Coordinates (ZMod q) d) := by
  intro x y z w
  ext i
  exact finiteBracket_tail (tail_trivial x)
    (finiteBracket_tail (tail_trivial y) (finiteBracket_tail (tail_trivial z) (tail_trivial w)))
    i (by have := i.isLt; omega)

private local instance instResidueClassThree (d q : ℕ) :
    Fact (ClassThree (Coordinates (ZMod q) d)) := ⟨finiteClassThree d q⟩

private abbrev Base (d q : ℕ) := BCH (Coordinates (ZMod q) d)

private local instance instFiniteBase (d q : ℕ) [NeZero q] : Finite (Base d q) :=
  Finite.of_injective BCH.val (fun x y h ↦ by cases x; cases y; cases h; rfl)

private theorem base_card (d q : ℕ) : Nat.card (Base d q) = q ^ (3 * d) := by
  let e : Base d q ≃ Coordinates (ZMod q) d :=
    ⟨BCH.val, BCH.mk, fun _ ↦ rfl, fun _ ↦ rfl⟩
  rw [Nat.card_congr e, Nat.card_fun, Nat.card_zmod, Nat.card_fin]

private theorem base_mul_coord {d q m n : ℕ} {x y : Base d q} (hx : Tail m x.val)
    (hy : Tail n y.val) {k : Fin (3 * d)} (hk : k.val < d + m + n) :
    (x * y).val k = x.val k + y.val k := by
  change bchMul x.val y.val k = _
  have hb := finiteBracket_tail hx hy
  have hb' := finiteBracket_tail hy hx
  have hx' := finiteBracket_tail (tail_trivial x.val) hb
  have hy' := finiteBracket_tail (tail_trivial y.val) hb'
  simp [bchMul, hb k hk, hx' k (by omega), hy' k (by omega)]

private theorem base_pow {d q : ℕ} (x : Base d q) (k : ℕ) : (x ^ k).val = k • x.val := by
  induction k with
  | zero => rw [pow_zero, zero_nsmul]; rfl
  | succ k ih =>
    rw [pow_succ]
    change bchMul (x ^ k).val x.val = (k + 1) • x.val
    simp only [ih, bchMul, nsmul_lie, lie_nsmul, lie_self, nsmul_zero, lie_zero,
      add_zero, add_nsmul, one_nsmul]

private theorem base_comm_tail {d q m n : ℕ} {x y : Base d q} (hx : Tail m x.val)
    (hy : Tail n y.val) : Tail (d + m + n) (⁅x, y⁆ : Base d q).val := by
  rw [bch_commutator]
  have hb := finiteBracket_tail hx hy
  exact tail_add (tail_nsmul hb _)
    (tail_nsmul (tail_of_le (by omega) (finiteBracket_tail (tail_trivial _) hb)) _)

private theorem base_comm_lead {d q : ℕ} {i j k : Fin (3 * d)} {x y : Base d q}
    (hx : Tail i.val x.val) (hy : Tail j.val y.val) (hk : k.val = d + i.val + j.val)
    (hd : 0 < d) :
    (⁅x, y⁆ : Base d q).val k =
      12 * x.val i * y.val j * ((integralTable d).entries i j k : ZMod q) := by
  rw [bch_commutator]
  have hb := finiteBracket_tail hx hy
  have hc := finiteBracket_tail (tail_trivial (x.val + y.val)) hb
  change (12 • (⁅x.val, y.val⁆ k) : ZMod q) +
    72 • (⁅x.val + y.val, ⁅x.val, y.val⁆⁆ k) = _
  have hlt : k.val < d + 0 + (d + i.val + j.val) := by
    rw [hk, add_zero]
    exact Nat.lt_add_of_pos_left hd
  rw [hc k hlt, nsmul_zero, add_zero, finiteBracket_lead hx hy hk, nsmul_eq_mul]
  push_cast
  ring

private theorem tail_step {R : Type*} [Zero R] {d n : ℕ} {x : Coordinates R d}
    (hx : Tail n x) : Tail (n + 1) (step x) := by
  intro k hk
  by_cases h : k.val = 0
  · simp [step, h]
  have hlt : k.val - 1 < n := by omega
  simp only [step, ite_eq_right h]
  exact hx ⟨k.val - 1, by omega⟩ hlt

private theorem step_succ {R : Type*} [Zero R] {d : ℕ} (x : Coordinates R d)
    (i : Fin (3 * d)) {h : i.val + 1 < 3 * d} : step x ⟨i.val + 1, h⟩ = x i := by
  simp [step]

private def translate (d q : ℕ) : Module.End (ZMod q) (Coordinates (ZMod q) d) :=
  1 + stepLin d

private theorem translate_apply {d q : ℕ} (x : Coordinates (ZMod q) d) :
    translate d q x = x + step x := rfl

private theorem translate_lie {d q : ℕ} (x y : Coordinates (ZMod q) d) :
    translate d q ⁅x, y⁆ = ⁅translate d q x, translate d q y⁆ := finiteBracket_shift x y

private theorem translate_injective (d q : ℕ) : Function.Injective (translate d q) := by
  intro x y h
  ext i
  suffices ∀ n : ℕ, ∀ hn : n < 3 * d, x ⟨n, hn⟩ = y ⟨n, hn⟩ by exact this i.val i.isLt
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro hn
    simpa [translate_apply, step] using congr_fun h ⟨0, hn⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    intro hn
    have hh := congr_fun h ⟨n + 1, hn⟩
    rw [translate_apply, translate_apply, Pi.add_apply, Pi.add_apply,
      step_succ _ ⟨n, by omega⟩, step_succ _ ⟨n, by omega⟩, ih (by omega)] at hh
    exact add_right_cancel hh

private def translateAut (d q : ℕ) [NeZero q] : MulAut (Base d q) := by
  let f : Base d q →* Base d q :=
    { toFun := fun x ↦ BCH.mk (translate d q x.val)
      map_one' := congrArg BCH.mk ((translate d q).map_zero)
      map_mul' := fun x y ↦ by
        apply congrArg BCH.mk
        change translate d q (bchMul x.val y.val) =
          bchMul (translate d q x.val) (translate d q y.val)
        simp only [bchMul, map_add, map_nsmul, translate_lie] }
  have hi : Function.Injective f := by
    intro x y h
    have h' := translate_injective d q (congrArg BCH.val h)
    cases x
    cases y
    cases h'
    rfl
  exact MulEquiv.ofBijective f (Finite.injective_iff_bijective.mp hi)

private theorem translateAut_val {d q : ℕ} [NeZero q] (x : Base d q) :
    (translateAut d q x).val = x.val + step x.val := rfl

private theorem shift_pow_tail {d q : ℕ} [NeZero q] {j : ℕ} {x : Base d q}
    (hx : Tail j x.val) (b : ℕ) : Tail (j + 1) (((translateAut d q ^ b) x).val - x.val) := by
  induction b with
  | zero => simpa using tail_zero (R := ZMod q) (d := d) (n := j + 1)
  | succ b ih =>
    rw [pow_succ', MulAut.mul_apply, translateAut_val]
    rw [show ((translateAut d q ^ b) x).val + step ((translateAut d q ^ b) x).val - x.val =
      (((translateAut d q ^ b) x).val - x.val) + step ((translateAut d q ^ b) x).val by abel]
    have h := tail_add (tail_of_le (Nat.le_succ j) ih) hx
    rw [sub_add_cancel] at h
    exact tail_add ih (tail_step h)

private theorem shift_pow_lead {d q : ℕ} [NeZero q] {i : Fin (3 * d)} {x : Base d q}
    (hx : Tail i.val x.val) (b : ℕ) (hi : i.val + 1 < 3 * d) :
    ((translateAut d q ^ b) x).val ⟨i.val + 1, hi⟩ - x.val ⟨i.val + 1, hi⟩ =
      (b : ZMod q) * x.val i := by
  induction b with
  | zero => simp
  | succ b ih =>
    rw [pow_succ', MulAut.mul_apply, translateAut_val, Pi.add_apply, step_succ _ i]
    have hh := shift_pow_tail hx b i (by omega)
    rw [sub_eq_zero.mp hh, Nat.cast_succ]
    linear_combination ih

private abbrev Cycle (d q b : ℕ) [NeZero q] := Subgroup.zpowers (translateAut d q ^ b)

private abbrev CounterGroup (d q b : ℕ) [NeZero q] :=
  (Base d q) ⋊[((Cycle d q b).subtype)] (Cycle d q b)

private local instance instFiniteCounterGroup (d q b : ℕ) [NeZero q] :
    Finite (CounterGroup d q b) :=
  Finite.of_equiv _ (SemidirectProduct.equivProd (φ := (Cycle d q b).subtype)).symm

private def cycleGen (d q b : ℕ) [NeZero q] : Cycle d q b :=
  ⟨translateAut d q ^ b, Subgroup.mem_zpowers _⟩

private theorem cycle_pow {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (c : Cycle d q b) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, cycleGen d q b ^ k = c := by
  have h := isOfFinOrder_of_finite (translateAut d q ^ b)
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h.mem_powers_iff_mem_zpowers.mpr c.2
  exact ⟨k, Subtype.ext hk⟩

private theorem cycle_action_tail {d q b n : ℕ} [NeZero q] (c : Cycle d q b)
    {x : Base d q} (hx : Tail n x.val) :
    Tail (n + 1) (((c : MulAut (Base d q)) x).val - x.val) := by
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := cycle_pow c
  change Tail (n + 1) ((((translateAut d q ^ b) ^ k) x).val - x.val)
  rw [← pow_mul]
  exact shift_pow_tail hx _

private theorem cycle_action_preserves {d q b n : ℕ} [NeZero q] (c : Cycle d q b)
    {x : Base d q} (hx : Tail n x.val) : Tail n ((c : MulAut (Base d q)) x).val := by
  have h := tail_add (tail_of_le (Nat.le_succ n) (cycle_action_tail c hx)) hx
  rwa [sub_add_cancel] at h

private def baseTail (d q n : ℕ) : Subgroup (Base d q) where
  carrier := {x | Tail n x.val}
  one_mem' := tail_zero
  mul_mem' {x y} hx hy := fun k hk ↦ by
    exact (base_mul_coord hx hy (by omega)).trans (by simp [hx k hk, hy k hk])
  inv_mem' hx := tail_neg hx

private abbrev embed {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] : Base d q →* CounterGroup d q b :=
  SemidirectProduct.inl

private abbrev embedCycle {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] : Cycle d q b →* CounterGroup d q b :=
  SemidirectProduct.inr

private def shell (d q b n : ℕ) [NeZero q] : Subgroup (CounterGroup d q b) :=
  (baseTail d q n).map embed

private theorem shell_embed_mem {d q b n : ℕ} [NeZero q] {x : Base d q} :
    (embed x : CounterGroup d q b) ∈ shell d q b n ↔ Tail n x.val := by
  rw [shell, Subgroup.mem_map]
  exact ⟨fun ⟨y, hy, he⟩ ↦ (SemidirectProduct.inl_injective he) ▸ hy, fun hx ↦ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩⟩

private theorem shell_mem_iff {d q b n : ℕ} [NeZero q] (g : CounterGroup d q b) :
    g ∈ shell d q b n ↔ g.right = 1 ∧ Tail n g.left.val := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨rfl, hx⟩
  · rintro ⟨hr, hx⟩
    have hg : embed g.left = g :=
      SemidirectProduct.ext rfl hr.symm
    exact ⟨g.left, hx, hg⟩

private theorem base_conj_tail {d q n : ℕ} (x : Base d q) {y : Base d q}
    (hy : Tail n y.val) : Tail n (x * y * x⁻¹).val := by
  have hc := tail_of_le (by omega : n ≤ d + 0 + n) (base_comm_tail (tail_trivial x.val) hy)
  have hm := (baseTail d q n).mul_mem hc hy
  rwa [commutatorElement_def, inv_mul_cancel_right] at hm

private def commShift {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (c : Cycle d q b) (x : Base d q) : Base d q :=
  ((c : MulAut (Base d q)) x) * x⁻¹

private theorem commShift_formula {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (c : Cycle d q b) (x : Base d q) :
    ⁅(embedCycle c : CounterGroup d q b), embed (b := b) x⁆ = embed (commShift c x) := by
  simp only [commutatorElement_def, commShift, map_mul, map_inv]
  rw [← map_inv, ← SemidirectProduct.inl_aut]
  rfl

private theorem commShift_tail {d q b n : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 0 < d) (c : Cycle d q b)
    {x : Base d q} (hx : Tail n x.val) : Tail (n + 1) (commShift c x).val := by
  intro i hi
  have hinv : Tail n (x⁻¹).val := tail_neg hx
  have hlt : i.val < d + n + n := hi.trans_le (by have := hd; omega)
  rw [commShift, base_mul_coord (cycle_action_preserves c hx) hinv hlt]
  change ((c : MulAut (Base d q)) x).val i + (-x.val i) = 0
  rw [← sub_eq_add_neg]
  exact cycle_action_tail c hx i hi

private theorem commShift_lead {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d) {i : Fin (3 * d)}
    {x : Base d q} (hx : Tail i.val x.val) (hi : i.val + 1 < 3 * d) :
    (commShift (cycleGen d q b) x).val ⟨i.val + 1, hi⟩ = (b : ZMod q) * x.val i := by
  have hinv : Tail i.val (x⁻¹).val := tail_neg hx
  have hk : (⟨i.val + 1, hi⟩ : Fin (3 * d)).val < d + i.val + i.val := by
    change i.val + 1 < d + i.val + i.val
    omega
  rw [commShift, base_mul_coord (cycle_action_preserves _ hx) hinv hk]
  change ((translateAut d q ^ b) x).val ⟨i.val + 1, hi⟩ + - x.val ⟨i.val + 1, hi⟩ = _
  rw [← sub_eq_add_neg]
  exact shift_pow_lead hx b hi

private theorem arbitrary_comm_shell {d q b n : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 0 < d)
    (g : CounterGroup d q b) {x : Base d q} (hx : Tail n x.val) :
    ⁅g, embed x⁆ ∈ shell d q b (n + 1) := by
  obtain ⟨w, c⟩ := g
  rw [SemidirectProduct.mk_eq_inl_mul_inr c w, commutatorElement_mul_left_eq_conj_mul,
    commShift_formula, ← map_commutatorElement, ← map_inv, ← map_mul, ← map_mul]
  apply (shell d q b (n + 1)).mul_mem
  · exact shell_embed_mem.mpr (base_conj_tail w (commShift_tail hd c hx))
  · exact shell_embed_mem.mpr
      (tail_of_le (by omega : n + 1 ≤ d + 0 + n) (base_comm_tail (tail_trivial w.val) hx))

private def firstCoord (d q b : ℕ) [NeZero q] (hd : 0 < d) :
    CounterGroup d q b →* Multiplicative (ZMod q) where
  toFun g := Multiplicative.ofAdd (g.left.val ⟨0, by omega⟩)
  map_one' := rfl
  map_mul' g h := by
    change (g.left * (g.right : MulAut (Base d q)) h.left).val _ = _
    rw [base_mul_coord (tail_trivial _) (tail_trivial _) (by omega : 0 < d + 0 + 0)]
    have hc := cycle_action_tail g.right (tail_trivial h.left.val) ⟨0, by omega⟩
      (by change 0 < 1; decide)
    have hce : ((g.right : MulAut (Base d q)) h.left).val ⟨0, by omega⟩ =
      h.left.val ⟨0, by omega⟩ := sub_eq_zero.mp hc
    rw [hce]
    rfl

private theorem comm_shell_one {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 0 < d)
    (g h : CounterGroup d q b) : ⁅g, h⁆ ∈ shell d q b 1 := by
  apply (shell_mem_iff _).mpr
  constructor
  · change (SemidirectProduct.rightHom ⁅g, h⁆) = 1
    rw [map_commutatorElement, commutatorElement_eq_one_iff_commute]
    let _ := IsCyclic.commGroup (α := Cycle d q b)
    exact Commute.all _ _
  · intro i hi
    have he : i = ⟨0, by omega⟩ := Fin.ext (by change i.val = 0; omega)
    rw [he]
    change Multiplicative.toAdd (firstCoord d q b hd ⁅g, h⁆) = 0
    rw [map_commutatorElement, (Commute.all _ _).commutator_eq]
    rfl

private theorem lower_le_shell {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 0 < d) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, (⊤ : Subgroup (CounterGroup d q b)).lowerCentralSeries (n + 1) ≤
      shell d q b (n + 1) := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    rw [Subgroup.lowerCentralSeries_succ, Subgroup.lowerCentralSeries_zero,
      Subgroup.commutator_le]
    exact fun g _ h _ ↦ comm_shell_one hd g h
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [Subgroup.lowerCentralSeries_succ, Subgroup.commutator_le]
    intro g hg h _
    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := ih hg
    rw [← commutatorElement_inv]
    exact (shell d q b (n + 2)).inv_mem (arbitrary_comm_shell hd h hx)

private def ladder (d q b : ℕ) [NeZero q] : ℕ → Base d q
  | 0 => BCH.mk (axis (ZMod q) d 0)
  | n + 1 => commShift (cycleGen d q b) (ladder d q b n)

private theorem ladder_tail {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d) (n : ℕ) :
    Tail n (ladder d q b n).val := by
  induction n with
  | zero => exact tail_trivial _
  | succ n ih => exact commShift_tail (by omega) _ ih

private theorem ladder_lead {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d) (n : ℕ)
    (hn : n < 3 * d) : (ladder d q b n).val ⟨n, hn⟩ = (b : ZMod q) ^ n := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [ladder, axis]
  | succ n ih =>
    change (commShift (cycleGen d q b) (ladder d q b n)).val ⟨n + 1, hn⟩ = _
    rw [commShift_lead hd (i := ⟨n, by omega⟩) (ladder_tail hd n) hn, ih, pow_succ']

private theorem ladder_mem_lower {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (n : ℕ) :
    (embed (ladder d q b n) : CounterGroup d q b) ∈
      (⊤ : Subgroup (CounterGroup d q b)).lowerCentralSeries n := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [ladder, ← commShift_formula, Subgroup.lowerCentralSeries_succ,
      ← commutatorElement_inv]
    exact Subgroup.inv_mem _ (Subgroup.commutator_mem_commutator ih (Subgroup.mem_top _))

private theorem leading_correction {d q b n : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d)
    (hb : IsUnit (b : ZMod q)) (hn : n < 3 * d) {x : Base d q} (hx : Tail n x.val) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, Tail (n + 1) (x * (ladder d q b n ^ k)⁻¹).val := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hb.pow n
  let a : ZMod q := x.val ⟨n, hn⟩ * ↑u⁻¹
  refine ⟨a.val, ?_⟩
  have hv : ((a.val : ℕ) : ZMod q) * (b : ZMod q) ^ n = x.val ⟨n, hn⟩ := by
    rw [ZMod.natCast_zmod_val, ← hu]
    simp [a, mul_assoc]
  have hpow : Tail n ((ladder d q b n ^ a.val)⁻¹).val := by
    change Tail n (-(ladder d q b n ^ a.val).val)
    rw [base_pow]
    exact tail_neg (tail_nsmul (ladder_tail hd n) _)
  intro i hi
  rw [base_mul_coord hx hpow (by omega)]
  change x.val i + -(ladder d q b n ^ a.val).val i = 0
  rw [← sub_eq_add_neg, base_pow]
  rcases lt_or_eq_of_le (Nat.le_of_lt_succ hi) with hlt | heq
  · simp [hx i hlt, ladder_tail hd n i hlt]
  · have h : i = ⟨n, hn⟩ := Fin.ext heq
    rw [h]
    change x.val ⟨n, hn⟩ - a.val • (ladder d q b n).val ⟨n, hn⟩ = 0
    rw [ladder_lead hd, nsmul_eq_mul, hv, sub_self]

private theorem shell_le_of_ladder {d q b m : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d)
    (hb : IsUnit (b : ZMod q)) {H : Subgroup (CounterGroup d q b)}
    (hH : ∀ n ≥ m, embed (ladder d q b n) ∈ H) : shell d q b m ≤ H := by
  suffices h : ∀ a n, 3 * d - n = a → m ≤ n → ∀ x : Base d q, Tail n x.val → embed x ∈ H by
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact h _ _ rfl le_rfl x hx
  intro a
  induction a using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | ind a ih =>
    intro n ha hmn x hx
    by_cases hn : n < 3 * d
    · obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := leading_correction hd hb hn hx
      have hz := ih (3 * d - (n + 1)) (by omega) (n + 1) rfl (by omega) _ hk
      rw [map_mul, map_inv, map_pow] at hz
      have hu := H.pow_mem (hH n hmn) k
      simpa using H.mul_mem hz hu
    · have hzero : x.val = 0 := funext fun i ↦ hx i (by have := i.isLt; omega)
      have he : x = 1 := by cases x; cases hzero; rfl
      simp [he]

private theorem lower_eq_shell {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d)
    (hb : IsUnit (b : ZMod q)) (m : ℕ) (hm : 1 ≤ m) :
    (⊤ : Subgroup (CounterGroup d q b)).lowerCentralSeries m = shell d q b m := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · cases m with
    | zero => omega
    | succ n => exact lower_le_shell (by omega) n
  · apply shell_le_of_ladder hd hb
    intro n hn
    exact (⊤ : Subgroup (CounterGroup d q b)).lowerCentralSeries_antitone hn
      (ladder_mem_lower n)

private theorem example_factors {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d)
    (hb : IsUnit (b : ZMod q)) :
    HasCyclicLowerCentralFactorsFromSecond (CounterGroup d q b) := by
  intro j hj
  rw [lower_eq_shell hd hb j hj, lower_eq_shell hd hb (j + 1) (by omega)]
  refine ⟨embed (ladder d q b j), shell_embed_mem.mpr (ladder_tail hd j), ?_⟩
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  by_cases hj' : j < 3 * d
  · obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := leading_correction hd hb hj' hx
    refine ⟨(k : ℤ), ?_⟩
    rw [zpow_natCast, ← map_pow, ← map_inv, ← map_mul]
    exact shell_embed_mem.mpr hk
  · refine ⟨0, ?_⟩
    rw [zpow_zero, inv_one, mul_one]
    apply shell_embed_mem.mpr
    exact fun i hi ↦ hx i (by have := i.isLt; omega)

private theorem example_two_generated {d q b : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d)
    (hb : IsUnit (b : ZMod q)) :
    ∃ x y : CounterGroup d q b, Subgroup.closure ({x, y} : Set (CounterGroup d q b)) = ⊤ := by
  let t : CounterGroup d q b := embedCycle (cycleGen d q b)
  let u : CounterGroup d q b := embed (ladder d q b 0)
  let H := Subgroup.closure ({t, u} : Set (CounterGroup d q b))
  have ht : t ∈ H := Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp : t ∈ ({t, u} : Set _))
  have hu : u ∈ H := Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp : u ∈ ({t, u} : Set _))
  have hL (n : ℕ) : embed (ladder d q b n) ∈ H := by
    induction n with
    | zero => exact hu
    | succ n ih =>
      rw [ladder, ← commShift_formula]
      exact H.mul_mem (H.mul_mem (H.mul_mem ht ih) (H.inv_mem ht)) (H.inv_mem ih)
  have hbase : shell d q b 0 ≤ H := shell_le_of_ladder hd hb fun n _ ↦ hL n
  refine ⟨t, u, eq_top_iff.mpr ?_⟩
  intro g _
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := cycle_pow g.right
  have hr : embedCycle g.right ∈ H := by
    rw [← hk, map_pow]
    exact H.pow_mem ht k
  rw [← SemidirectProduct.inl_left_mul_inr_right g]
  exact H.mul_mem (hbase (shell_embed_mem.mpr (tail_trivial _))) hr

private theorem exists_p_group_parameter (d p a : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (ha : 0 < a)
    [NeZero (p ^ a)] :
    ∃ b : ℕ, IsUnit (b : ZMod (p ^ a)) ∧ IsPGroup p (CounterGroup d (p ^ a) b) := by
  let T := translateAut d (p ^ a)
  let b := ordCompl[p] (orderOf T)
  have hN : orderOf T ≠ 0 := (orderOf_pos T).ne'
  refine ⟨b, (ZMod.isUnit_natCast_iff_not_dvd_pow hp ha).mpr (Nat.not_dvd_ordCompl hp hN), ?_⟩
  have hT : (T ^ b) ^ (p ^ (orderOf T).factorization p) = 1 := by
    rw [← pow_mul, mul_comm b, Nat.ordProj_mul_ordCompl_eq_self]
    exact pow_orderOf_eq_one _
  apply IsPGroup.of_card_dvd_pow (n := a * (3 * d) + (orderOf T).factorization p)
  rw [SemidirectProduct.card, base_card, ← pow_mul, pow_add, Nat.card_zpowers]
  exact Nat.mul_dvd_mul_left _ (orderOf_dvd_of_pow_eq_one hT)

/-! ## The rank obstruction -/

section

variable {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G]

private theorem generators_attained (H : Subgroup G) :
    ∃ s : Finset G, s.card = minGenerators H ∧ Subgroup.closure (s : Set G) = H := by
  classical
  let := Fintype.ofFinite G
  let s := Finset.univ.filter (· ∈ H)
  have hs : (s : Set G) = (H : Set G) := by ext x; simp [s]
  let S : Set ℕ := {n | ∃ t : Finset G, t.card = n ∧ Subgroup.closure (t : Set G) = H}
  have hS : S.Nonempty := ⟨s.card, s, rfl, by rw [hs, Subgroup.closure_eq]⟩
  exact csInf_mem hS

private theorem groupRank_bdd : BddAbove (Set.range (minGenerators (G := G))) := by
  classical
  let := Fintype.ofFinite G
  refine ⟨Fintype.card G, ?_⟩
  rintro k ⟨H, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨s, hs, _⟩ := generators_attained H
  exact hs ▸ Finset.card_le_univ s

private theorem subgroup_rank_le_groupRank (H : Subgroup G) :
    Group.rank H ≤ groupRank G := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hclosure⟩ := generators_attained H
  calc
    Group.rank H ≤ s.card := hclosure ▸ Subgroup.rank_closure_finset_le_card s
    _ = minGenerators H := hs
    _ ≤ groupRank G := le_csSup groupRank_bdd ⟨H, rfl⟩

private theorem card_section_le {A : Type*} [CommGroup A] [Finite A]
    (H : Subgroup G) (f : H →* A) (hf : Function.Surjective f) {e r : ℕ}
    (he : Monoid.exponent A ∣ e) (hpos : 0 < e) (hr : groupRank G ≤ r) :
    Nat.card A ≤ e ^ r := by
  have hle : Group.rank A ≤ r :=
    (Group.rank_le_of_surjective f hf).trans ((subgroup_rank_le_groupRank H).trans hr)
  have hdiv := (card_dvd_exponent_pow_rank A).trans (pow_dvd_pow_of_dvd he _)
  exact (Nat.le_of_dvd (pow_pos hpos _) hdiv).trans (Nat.pow_le_pow_right hpos hle)

omit [Finite G] in
private theorem triple_eq_one {N : Subgroup G} (hN : N.lowerCentralSeries 2 = ⊥)
    {x y z : G} (hx : x ∈ N) (hy : y ∈ N) (hz : z ∈ N) : ⁅⁅x, y⁆, z⁆ = 1 := by
  have h := Subgroup.commutator_mem_commutator (Subgroup.commutator_mem_commutator hx hy) hz
  change ⁅⁅x, y⁆, z⁆ ∈ N.lowerCentralSeries 2 at h
  rw [hN] at h
  exact Subgroup.mem_bot.mp h

private theorem small_coefficient_cast_zero {p b : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) {c : ℤ}
    (hc : c ≠ 0) (hc' : c.natAbs < p ^ b) (x : ZMod (p ^ (4 * b)))
    (hx : (c : ZMod (p ^ (4 * b))) * x ^ 3 = 0) :
    ZMod.castHom (pow_dvd_pow p (by omega : b ≤ 4 * b)) (ZMod (p ^ b)) x = 0 := by
  have : NeZero (p ^ (4 * b)) := ⟨pow_ne_zero _ hp.ne_zero⟩
  let a := x.val
  have hxa : (a : ZMod (p ^ (4 * b))) = x := ZMod.natCast_zmod_val x
  have ha : p ^ b ∣ a := by
    by_cases ha0 : a = 0
    · simp [ha0]
    by_contra h
    have h₁ : c.natAbs.factorization p < b := by
      by_contra! hh
      exact (not_le.mpr hc') (Nat.le_of_dvd
        (Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hc) ((hp.pow_dvd_iff_le_factorization
          (Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hc).ne').mpr hh))
    have h₂ : a.factorization p < b := by
      by_contra! hh
      exact h ((hp.pow_dvd_iff_le_factorization ha0).mpr hh)
    have hh : (p ^ (4 * b) : ℤ) ∣ c * (a : ℤ) ^ 3 := by
      apply (ZMod.intCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd _ _).mp
      push_cast
      rw [hxa, hx]
    have hh' : p ^ (4 * b) ∣ c.natAbs * a ^ 3 := by
      simpa only [Int.natAbs_mul, Int.natAbs_pow, Int.natAbs_natCast] using
        Int.natAbs_dvd_natAbs.mpr hh
    have h₃ := (hp.pow_dvd_iff_le_factorization
      (Nat.mul_ne_zero (Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hc).ne' (pow_ne_zero _ ha0))).mp hh'
    rw [Nat.factorization_mul (Int.natAbs_pos.mpr hc).ne' (pow_ne_zero _ ha0),
      Nat.factorization_pow, Finsupp.add_apply, Finsupp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul] at h₃
    omega
  rw [← hxa, map_natCast, ZMod.natCast_eq_zero_iff]
  exact ha

private theorem card_box_le_quotient {p b m : ℕ} [NeZero (p ^ (4 * b))]
    (U : AddSubgroup (Fin m → ZMod (p ^ (4 * b))))
    (hU : ∀ u ∈ U, ∀ j : Fin m, (∀ i : Fin m, i.val < j.val → u i = 0) →
      ZMod.castHom (pow_dvd_pow p (by omega : b ≤ 4 * b)) (ZMod (p ^ b)) (u j) = 0) :
    (p ^ b) ^ m ≤ Nat.card ((Fin m → ZMod (p ^ (4 * b))) ⧸ U) := by
  let f : (Fin m → Fin (p ^ b)) → ((Fin m → ZMod (p ^ (4 * b))) ⧸ U) :=
    fun v ↦ QuotientAddGroup.mk' U (fun j ↦ ((v j).val : ZMod (p ^ (4 * b))))
  have hf : Function.Injective f := by
    intro v w hvw
    have hmem : ((fun j : Fin m ↦ ((v j).val : ZMod (p ^ (4 * b)))) -
        (fun j : Fin m ↦ ((w j).val : ZMod (p ^ (4 * b))))) ∈ U := by
      rw [← QuotientAddGroup.eq_iff_sub_mem]
      exact hvw
    ext j
    suffices ∀ k : ℕ, ∀ hk : k < m, v ⟨k, hk⟩ = w ⟨k, hk⟩ by
      exact congrArg Fin.val (this j.val j.isLt)
    intro k
    induction k using Nat.strong_induction_on with
    | ind k ih =>
      intro hk
      have hzero := hU _ hmem ⟨k, hk⟩ (fun i hi ↦ by simp [ih i.val hi i.isLt])
      simp only [Pi.sub_apply, map_sub, map_natCast, sub_eq_zero] at hzero
      apply Fin.ext
      simpa only [ZMod.val_natCast_of_lt (v ⟨k, hk⟩).isLt,
        ZMod.val_natCast_of_lt (w ⟨k, hk⟩).isLt] using congrArg ZMod.val hzero
  simpa [Nat.card_fun] using Nat.card_le_card_of_injective f hf

end

private def lowProj (d q m : ℕ) (hm : m ≤ d) :
    Base d q →* Multiplicative (Fin m → ZMod q) where
  toFun x := Multiplicative.ofAdd (fun i ↦ x.val ⟨i.val, by omega⟩)
  map_one' := rfl
  map_mul' x y := congrArg Multiplicative.ofAdd <| funext fun i ↦
    base_mul_coord (tail_trivial x.val) (tail_trivial y.val)
      (show i.val < d + 0 + 0 by have := i.isLt; omega)

private theorem lowProj_surjective (d q m : ℕ) (hm : m ≤ d) :
    Function.Surjective (lowProj d q m hm) := by
  intro a
  let x : Base d q := BCH.mk fun i ↦ if h : i.val < m then a.toAdd ⟨i.val, h⟩ else 0
  refine ⟨x, congrArg Multiplicative.ofAdd (funext fun i ↦ ?_)⟩
  change x.val ⟨i.val, by omega⟩ = a.toAdd i
  simp [x, i.isLt]

private def detectionCoeff {d m : ℕ} (hm : 3 * m ≤ d) (j : Fin m) : ℤ :=
  let i : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨j.val, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩
  let i' : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨j.val + 1, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩
  let k : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨d + i.val + i'.val, by dsimp [i, i']; have := j.isLt; omega⟩
  let l : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨d + k.val + i.val, by dsimp [i, i', k]; have := j.isLt; omega⟩
  144 * (integralTable d).entries i i' k * (integralTable d).entries k i l

private theorem detectionCoeff_ne {d m : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d) (hm : 3 * m ≤ d) (j : Fin m) :
    detectionCoeff hm j ≠ 0 := by
  dsimp only [detectionCoeff]
  apply mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero (by decide) ?_) ?_
  · exact (integralTable d).leading hd _ _ _ rfl (fun h ↦ by
      have := congrArg Fin.val h
      simp at this)
  · exact (integralTable d).leading hd _ _ _ rfl (fun h ↦ by
      have h' := congrArg Fin.val h
      change d + j.val + (j.val + 1) = j.val at h'
      omega)

private theorem triple_detect {d q b m : ℕ} [NeZero q] (hd : 2 ≤ d)
    (hm : 3 * m ≤ d) (j : Fin m) {x : Base d q} (hx : Tail j.val x.val) :
    (⁅⁅x, commShift (cycleGen d q b) x⁆, x⁆ : Base d q).val
      ⟨2 * d + 3 * j.val + 1, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩ =
        (b : ZMod q) * ((detectionCoeff hm j : ℤ) : ZMod q) *
          x.val ⟨j.val, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩ ^ 3 := by
  let i : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨j.val, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩
  let i' : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨j.val + 1, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩
  let k : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨d + i.val + i'.val, by dsimp [i, i']; have := j.isLt; omega⟩
  let l : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨2 * d + 3 * j.val + 1, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩
  let y := commShift (cycleGen d q b) x
  have hy : Tail i'.val y.val := commShift_tail (by omega) _ hx
  change (⁅⁅x, y⁆, x⁆ : Base d q).val l =
    (b : ZMod q) * ((detectionCoeff hm j : ℤ) : ZMod q) * x.val i ^ 3
  have hl : l.val = d + k.val + i.val := by dsimp [l, k, i, i']; omega
  have hxy : Tail k.val (⁅x, y⁆ : Base d q).val := base_comm_tail hx hy
  rw [base_comm_lead hxy hx hl (by omega), base_comm_lead hx hy (k := k) rfl (by omega)]
  rw [show y.val i' = (b : ZMod q) * x.val i from
    commShift_lead (q := q) (b := b) (i := i) hd hx i'.isLt]
  simp only [detectionCoeff, Int.cast_mul, Int.cast_ofNat]
  let l' : Fin (3 * d) := ⟨d + k.val + i.val, hl ▸ l.isLt⟩
  change _ = (b : ZMod q) *
    (144 * ((integralTable d).entries i i' k : ZMod q) *
      ((integralTable d).entries k i l' : ZMod q)) * x.val i ^ 3
  rw [show l' = l from Fin.ext hl.symm]
  ring

private theorem base_exponent {d q : ℕ} (x : Base d q) : x ^ q = 1 := by
  have h : (x ^ q).val = (1 : Base d q).val := by
    rw [base_pow]
    ext i
    change q • x.val i = 0
    simp [nsmul_eq_mul]
  exact congrArg BCH.mk h

private theorem quotient_rank_large {d p a b m r : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (ha : 0 < a)
    (hd : 2 ≤ d) (hm : 3 * m ≤ d) (hr : 4 * r < m)
    (hcoeff : ∀ j : Fin m, (detectionCoeff hm j).natAbs < p ^ a)
    [NeZero (p ^ (4 * a))] (hb : IsUnit (b : ZMod (p ^ (4 * a))))
    (N : Subgroup (CounterGroup d (p ^ (4 * a)) b)) [hN : N.Normal]
    (hc : N.lowerCentralSeries 2 = ⊥) : ¬ groupRank (CounterGroup d (p ^ (4 * a)) b ⧸ N) ≤ r := by
  let q := p ^ (4 * a)
  let P := CounterGroup d q b
  let F : Base d q →* P := embed
  let π := lowProj d q m (show m ≤ d by omega)
  let U := ((N.comap F).map π).toAddSubgroup'
  have hU : ∀ u ∈ U, ∀ j : Fin m, (∀ i : Fin m, i.val < j.val → u i = 0) →
      ZMod.castHom (pow_dvd_pow p (by omega : a ≤ 4 * a)) (ZMod (p ^ a)) (u j) = 0 := by
    intro u hu j hj
    change Multiplicative.ofAdd u ∈ (N.comap F).map π at hu
    obtain ⟨x, hxN, he⟩ := hu
    change F x ∈ N at hxN
    have hx : Tail j.val x.val := by
      intro i hi
      have H := hj ⟨i.val, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩ hi
      have E := congrFun (congrArg Multiplicative.toAdd he) ⟨i.val, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩
      exact E.trans H
    let t : P := embedCycle (cycleGen d q b)
    let y := commShift (cycleGen d q b) x
    have hxy : F y ∈ N := by
      rw [show F y = ⁅t, F x⁆ from (commShift_formula _ _).symm]
      exact N.mul_mem (hN.conj_mem _ hxN t) (N.inv_mem hxN)
    have htr : ⁅⁅x, y⁆, x⁆ = 1 := by
      apply SemidirectProduct.inl_injective (φ := (Cycle d q b).subtype)
      change F ⁅⁅x, y⁆, x⁆ = F 1
      rw [map_commutatorElement, map_commutatorElement, map_one]
      exact triple_eq_one hc hxN hxy hxN
    have hdet := triple_detect hd hm j (b := b) hx
    change (⁅⁅x, y⁆, x⁆ : Base d q).val _ = _ at hdet
    rw [htr] at hdet
    have hz : ((detectionCoeff hm j : ℤ) : ZMod q) * x.val
        ⟨j.val, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩ ^ 3 = 0 := by
      apply hb.mul_left_cancel
      rw [← mul_assoc, ← hdet, mul_zero]
      rfl
    have E := congrFun (congrArg Multiplicative.toAdd he) j
    change x.val ⟨j.val, by have := j.isLt; omega⟩ = u j at E
    rw [← E]
    exact small_coefficient_cast_zero hp (detectionCoeff_ne hd hm j) (hcoeff j) _ hz
  let A := Multiplicative ((Fin m → ZMod q) ⧸ U)
  let f : Base d q →* A := (QuotientAddGroup.mk' U).toMultiplicative.comp π
  have hf : Function.Surjective f :=
    (QuotientAddGroup.mk'_surjective U).comp (lowProj_surjective d q m (by omega))
  let g := (QuotientGroup.mk' N).comp F
  have hker : g.ker ≤ f.ker := by
    intro x hx
    have hmem : F x ∈ N := (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff (F x)).mp hx
    change (QuotientAddGroup.mk' U) (π x).toAdd = 0
    apply (QuotientAddGroup.eq_zero_iff _).mpr
    exact ⟨x, hmem, rfl⟩
  let s : g.range →* A :=
    (QuotientGroup.lift g.ker f hker).comp (QuotientGroup.quotientKerEquivRange g).symm.toMonoidHom
  have hs : Function.Surjective s := (QuotientGroup.lift_surjective_of_surjective _ _ hf hker).comp
    (QuotientGroup.quotientKerEquivRange g).symm.surjective
  have he : Monoid.exponent A ∣ q := Monoid.exponent_dvd.mpr fun u ↦ by
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hf u
    apply orderOf_dvd_of_pow_eq_one
    rw [← map_pow, base_exponent, map_one]
  intro h
  have h₁ := card_box_le_quotient U hU
  have h₂ := card_section_le g.range s hs he (pow_pos hp.pos _) h
  have hle : (p ^ a) ^ m ≤ (p ^ (4 * a)) ^ r := h₁.trans h₂
  rw [← pow_mul, ← pow_mul] at hle
  have hle' := (pow_right_strictMono₀ hp.one_lt).le_iff_le.mp hle
  have hh : 4 * a * r = a * (4 * r) := by ring
  rw [hh] at hle'
  exact (not_le_of_gt (Nat.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left hr ha)) hle'

/--
**No rank analogue of the Shepherd-Leedham-Green-McKay theorem (Kourovka 16.103).** For every
prime $p$ and every natural number $r$ there is a finite $p$-group $P$ generated by two elements,
whose lower central factors $\gamma_i(P)/\gamma_{i+1}(P)$ are cyclic for all $i \ge 2$, such that
for every normal subgroup $N$ of $P$ of nilpotency class at most $2$ the quotient $P/N$ has rank
greater than $r$. Here $\gamma_1(P) = P$ and $\gamma_{i+1}(P) = [\gamma_i(P), P]$, and the rank of
a finite group is the largest minimal number of generators of its subgroups. That is, the
statement of Kourovka Problem 16.103 fails for every prime.

Khukhro's groups even have no normal subgroup of bounded derived length with quotient of bounded
rank; the Kourovka Archive answers 16.103 "No".

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group
Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems,
Problem 16.103 (E. I. Khukhro); resolution: E. I. Khukhro, Counterexamples to a rank analogue of the
Shepherd-Leedham-Green-McKay theorem on finite p-groups of maximal class, Siberian Math. J. 54
(2013), no. 1, 174-184, Theorem (no functions r(p), l(p) give every such group a normal subgroup of
derived length at most l(p) with quotient of rank at most r(p)), with examples for every fixed prime
(Section 4); Kourovka Archive, Problem 16.103 (answer: No),
https://eprints.maths.manchester.ac.uk/1937/1/.
-/
public theorem rankAnalogueMaximalClass_refuted : ¬ rankAnalogueMaximalClass := by
  rintro ⟨p, hp, r, h⟩
  let m := 4 * r + 1
  let d := 3 * m
  have hm : 3 * m ≤ d := le_rfl
  have hd : 2 ≤ d := by dsimp [d, m]; omega
  let a := 1 + ∑ j : Fin m, (detectionCoeff hm j).natAbs
  have ha : 0 < a := by dsimp [a]; omega
  have hcoeff (j : Fin m) : (detectionCoeff hm j).natAbs < p ^ a :=
    calc
      (detectionCoeff hm j).natAbs ≤ ∑ k : Fin m, (detectionCoeff hm k).natAbs :=
        Finset.single_le_sum (f := fun k ↦ (detectionCoeff hm k).natAbs)
          (fun k _ ↦ Nat.zero_le _) (Finset.mem_univ j)
      _ ≤ a := by dsimp [a]; omega
      _ < 2 ^ a := Nat.lt_two_pow_self
      _ ≤ p ^ a := Nat.pow_le_pow_left hp.two_le _
  have : NeZero (p ^ (4 * a)) := ⟨pow_ne_zero _ hp.ne_zero⟩
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hP⟩ := exists_p_group_parameter d p (4 * a) hp (by omega)
  obtain ⟨N, nNormal, hN, hr⟩ := h (CounterGroup d (p ^ (4 * a)) b) hP
    (example_two_generated hd hb) (example_factors hd hb)
  exact quotient_rank_large hp ha hd hm (Nat.lt_succ_self _) hcoeff hb N hN hr


end

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.RankAnalogueMaximalClassKourovka16Problem103Wanted
